      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/westport_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Westport is named after John West, a Scottish millwright and lumberman who settled in the area during the early 1850s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westport%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "John West founded the first salmon cannery on the Oregon side of the Columbia River in 1868.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/westport_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Westport Lumber Company once exported massive old-growth Douglas fir logs to destinations including Australia, Japan, and Europe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
